menu "micro:bit build client (mb_build_client)"

    config MB_BUILD_SERVICE_URL
        string "Build service URL for POST /v1/build"
        default "http://127.0.0.1:8477/v1/build"
        help
            The client appends ?region2=true, so the reply is the region-2 byte
            stream with the geometry in headers — the same shape /v1/speak
            returns. The device never handles the 1.8 MB base64 hex.

    config MB_BUILD_MAX_BYTES
        int "Region-2 receive buffer, allocated in PSRAM"
        default 49152
        help
            48 KB is the whole region-2 window of a micro:bit v1 (0x30000-0x3BBFF),
            so no legal image can overflow it. A smaller buffer is fine for the
            current payload (6 KB) but turns a bigger program into a rejection.

    config MB_BUILD_IP_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Seconds to wait for a WiFi address before giving up"
        default 60
        range 5 300
        help
            WiFi is brought up by mb_voice; this client only waits for the
            station to have an address before it posts.

endmenu
